.TH DIPIRIST 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipirist \- bridge a DVB-IPI stream between RTP/UDP/file and a RIST link, sender or receiver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipirist
.B \-i
.I uri
.B \-o
.I uri
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipirist
bridges a DVB-IPI stream between a plain RTP/UDP/file endpoint and a RIST
link (VSF TR-06), in either direction, using librist. RIST is not part of
DVB-IPI; this tool exists to carry DVB-IPI streams over unmanaged or lossy
networks with RIST's retransmission-based recovery.
.PP
Exactly one of
.B \-i
(input) or
.B \-o
(output) must be a
.B rist://
URI, the other is a regular
.BR dipirec (1)-style
endpoint: RTP or plain UDP multicast, a udpxy proxy (source side only),
stdin/stdout, or a file. Whether
.B dipirist
runs as a RIST sender or receiver follows from which side the
.B rist://
URI is on: a
.B rist://
output calls out to a receiver, a
.B rist://
input listens for a sender. Only one direction is served per process.
.PP
A
.B rist://
endpoint address is either
.IB host : port
(calls out) or
.BI @ host : port
(listens); the leading
.B @
mirrors this toolkit's own
.BR rtp://@ / udp://@
convention. Repeating
.B \-i
or
.B \-o
with further
.B rist://
URIs bonds several links carrying the same stream. RIST query parameters
such as \fBbuffer\fR, \fBsecret\fR, \fBcname\fR, and \fBweight\fR are
accepted directly in the URI; the equivalent command-line options below
override whatever the URI specifies.
.PP
RIST-specific concepts exposed on the command line: the
.B profile
(simple or main, main adds encryption), a pre-shared key
.RB ( secret ,
requires profile main), an RTCP
.B cname
identifying the stream, and the recovery
.B buffer
size in milliseconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-in " " \fIuri\fR
Input endpoint. Repeatable if it is a
.B rist://
URI, to bond several links.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIuri\fR
Output endpoint. Repeatable if it is a
.B rist://
URI, to bond several links.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " " \fIiface\fR
Interface for the non-RIST side's multicast join or send.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fIname\fR
RIST profile,
.B simple
or
.BR main .
Default
.BR simple .
.B main
adds encryption.
.TP
.B \-\-secret \fIpsk\fR
Pre-shared key for encryption. Requires
.BR \-\-profile\ main .
.TP
.B \-\-cname \fIname\fR
RTCP cname. Default is library-generated.
.TP
.B \-\-buffer \fIms\fR
RIST recovery buffer size in milliseconds (sets both min and max). Default
is the library default.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
Colorize log output:
.BR auto ,
.BR always ,
or
.BR never .
Default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket path for metrics output. Default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id for metrics. Metrics are disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Metrics snapshot interval in seconds. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print periodic bridge statistics on stderr.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipirist \-i rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000 \-o rist://1.2.3.4:6000 \-\-buffer 1000
Sender: read an RTP multicast and send it over RIST to a listening receiver.
.TP
.B dipirist \-i rist://@0.0.0.0:6000 \-o rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000 \-\-buffer 1000
Receiver: listen for an incoming RIST connection and re-emit as RTP
multicast.
.TP
.B dipirist \-i rtp://@239.1.1.1:5000 \-o rist://1.2.3.4:6000 \-o rist://5.6.7.8:6000
Bonded sender: the same stream carried over two independent RIST links.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
Non-zero on argument errors or I/O/network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipirec (1),
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1)
.PP
